PN,38106
SC,0006
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F381A1785424693
OL,3,CDrought declared: The South's parched
OL,4,Clandscape from the air
OL,6,FThe Country Land and Business
OL,7,FAssociation said: "Farmers are telling
OL,8,Fus this is the worst harvest in years.
OL,9,FA sodden winter followed by drought
OL,10,Fhas left wheat at half its usual
OL,11,Fheight and some crops not worth
OL,12,Fharvesting. Farmers are not
OL,13,Finvincible."
OL,15,FHampshire-based farmer, Will Atkinson,
OL,16,Fhas had to diversify in order to keep
OL,17,Fhis business going. He said: "The
OL,18,Fharvest has been accelerated by at
OL,19,Fleast a month because of this dry
OL,20,Fweather. The quality of our barley is
OL,21,Fquite poor, it's really shriveled up.
OL,26,@oD@SOUuD@LO]
OL,1,W~s1x0~s1~s hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}   G6/9
